// ============================================================================
// Hero of the Overworld: game data index
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Content is split into one RON file per entity under assets/data/ (enemies/,
// characters/, skills/, levels/, and so on), with each level's tilemaps kept as
// CSV files in maps/<level>/. This file only lists the starting party and the
// level order. To add a new party member or enemy, drop a file into the right
// folder (and register its texture key in src/data.rs). No engine or battle
// code needs to change.
//
// Sprite sheets are 16x16 grids. Animation clips select a `row` and a run of
// `frames` starting at `first_col`, played at `fps`.
//   swordsman.png : 5 cols x 12 rows. rows 0-3 = walk down/up/right/left,
//                   rows 4-7 = attack down/up/right/left.
//   mage.png      : 6 cols x 8 rows. rows 0-3 = walk down/up/right/left
//                   (4 frames), rows 4-7 = cast down/up/LEFT/RIGHT (5 frames;
//                   note the cast rows swap left/right vs. the walk rows).
//   demon.png     : 6 cols x 8 rows.
// ============================================================================
Meta(
    starting_party: ["swordsman"],
    // Levels in progression order (each unlocks the next). Index-sensitive:
    // screen neighbor links and auto-advance step through this order.
    // Chapter 1: greenwood through demonfacility (the DEMON KING ends chapter 1).
    // Chapter 2: castawayshore (where the party washes up after being flung to the
    // surface), then harborwatch, a peaceful garrison town they sail to in order
    // to rally soldiers. Chapter is a per-level field; the map shows one chapter
    // at a time.
    levels: ["greenwood", "stonepass", "travelersend", "demonfortress", "charreddepths", "demonfacility", "castawayshore", "harborwatch"],
)
